 "final_message": "All 12 work items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the 2 new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** I changed the functions in `metrics.py`, `loader.py` and `report.py` to match SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added one test for `None` counting as not converted, and one for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, `conversions_in_window` now says it sums the last `days` entries, and `daily_conversion_counts` has its own entry.\n- **Item 12:** The rest of the package also deviated from the spec, so I fixed it:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups, breaks ties by group name, and uses the section 8 ordering.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now gives `None` for an empty group and sorts the keys.\n  - `longest_positive_streak` now resets the run when a count is zero. Before, it never reset.\n  - I also changed the README's `dedupe_sessions` entry, which only said it \"removes duplicate sessions\", to say it keeps the last session per id, sorted by day then id.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with a `converted` value that isn't `1`, `0` or empty. I made `parse_session_log` raise `ValueError` with the line number in that case.\n\nI didn't add tests for the other sections.",
